msgid "class mlib.maths.quaternion.Quaternion"
msgstr "class mlib.maths.quaternion.Quaternion"

msgid "ベースクラス: :py:obj:`maya.api.OpenMaya.MQuaternion`"
msgstr "Base class: :py:obj:`maya.api.OpenMaya.MQuaternion`"

msgid "om2.MQuaternion を継承した XYZW 成分の可変な四元数。"
msgstr "A mutable quaternion with XYZW components that inherits from om2.MQuaternion."

msgid "``om2.MQuaternion`` の派生クラスなので、そのまま OpenMaya API 2.0 の関数へ 渡せる。コンストラクタは ``Quaternion()`` (単位四元数)、 ``Quaternion(x, y, z, w)``、``Quaternion([x, y, z, w])``、 ``Quaternion(MQuaternion)``、``Quaternion(angle, axis)`` (軸角。axis は MVector 系)、``Quaternion(a, b[, factor])`` (MVector a を b へ回す回転)など om2 と同じ形を受け付け、加えて ``Quaternion(x=0, y=0, z=0, w=1)`` の キーワード引数(省略した成分は単位四元数の値)も使える。成分は数値だけで、 不正な引数は om2 と同じく ValueError。生成時や積の計算時に正規化は行わない。"
msgstr "Since it is a subclass of ``om2.MQuaternion``, it can be passed directly to OpenMaya API 2.0 functions. The constructor accepts the same forms as om2, such as ``Quaternion()`` (unit quaternion), ``Quaternion(x, y, z, w)``, ``Quaternion([x, y, z, w])``, ``Quaternion(MQuaternion)``, ``Quaternion(angle, axis)`` (axis-angle; axis is MVector type), ``Quaternion(a, b[, factor])`` (rotation from vector a to b), etc., and additionally supports the keyword argument ``Quaternion(x=0, y=0, z=0, w=1)`` (if omitted components take unit quaternion values). The components are numeric only, and invalid arguments raise ValueError as in om2. Normalization is not performed during creation or when computing products."

msgid "積 ``q1 * q2`` は om2 と同じ順序で、q1 を先に適用してから q2 を適用する回転 になる(``(q1 * q2).asMatrix()`` は ``q1.asMatrix() * q2.asMatrix()`` と同じ回転。Hamilton 積の ``q2 ⊗ q1`` に等しい)。``+``、``-``、単項の ``-`` は om2 の成分ごとの演算。 ``数値 * q`` は om2 と同じく4成分のスカラー倍(``q * 数値`` と ``/`` は om2 と 同じく未対応)。演算結果は mlib の :class:`Quaternion` で返す(``om2.MQuaternion`` が 左辺でも同じ)。ただし ``om2.MEulerRotation * q`` は om2 側が先に処理するため ``om2.MEulerRotation`` になる(``EulerRotate * q`` は EulerRotate)。``*=`` / ``+=`` / ``-=`` は自身を書き換える(om2 の MQuaternion に無い ``+=`` / ``-=`` も mlib で in-place にしている)。"
msgstr "The product ``q1 * q2`` results in a rotation where q1 is applied before q2, following the same order as om2. ``(q1 * q2).asMatrix()`` is equivalent to ``q1.asMatrix() * q2.asMatrix()`` in rotation, and equal to the ``q2 ⊗ q1`` of Hamilton product. ``+``, ``-``, and unary ``-`` correspond to component-wise operations in om2. ``数値 * q`` represents scalar multiplication with a 4-component vector, same as in om2 (``q * 数値`` and ``/`` are unsupported, just like in om2). The result of the operation is returned by :class:`Quaternion` in mlib (same applies when ``om2.MQuaternion`` is on the left side). However, ``om2.MEulerRotation * q`` results in ``om2.MEulerRotation`` because processing occurs in the order of om2 side first (``EulerRotate * q`` refers to EulerRotate). ``*=`` / ``+=`` / ``-=`` modify themselves in place (mlib also implements in-place ``+=`` / ``-=``, which are not present in om2's MQuaternion)."

msgid "値は可変で成分へ代入でき、ハッシュは不可。``len()`` は 4、添字(-4〜3。範囲外は IndexError。スライスは成分の tuple)と反復は X、Y、Z、W の順。``==`` は成分の 完全一致で(``q`` と ``-q`` は同じ回転でも等しくない)、MQuaternion 系以外との 比較は :class:`~mlib.maths.vector.Vector` と同じく例外にしない。"
msgstr "Values are mutable and can be assigned to components, but hashes are immutable. ``len()`` is 4, with indices ranging from -4 to 3 (out-of-range access raises IndexError; slices return tuples of components). Iteration proceeds in the order X, Y, Z, W. ``==`` performs exact matching of components (even if ``q`` and ``-q`` represent the same rotation, they are not equal). Comparisons with non-MQuaternion types do not raise exceptions, as is the case with :class:`~mlib.maths.vector.Vector`."

